# libFuzzer's working corpus. Deliberately NOT committed, and deliberately
# separate from `seeds/`, which is.
#
# libFuzzer writes every newly interesting input into the first corpus
# directory it is given, so committing that directory would make `cargo fuzz
# run` dirty the working tree on every invocation and would silently grow the
# repository by a few megabytes a week. `seeds/` is the curated, committed set
# and is passed second, where libFuzzer reads but never writes.
#
# CI caches this directory across runs (see the `fuzz` job in
# `.github/workflows/ci.yml`): a 60-second run that starts from a cold corpus
# re-derives the same shallow inputs every time and never gets past them.
corpus/

# Where libFuzzer writes the input that crashed. A genuine crash's input
# belongs in `seeds/<target>/` as a named regression case, committed, with
# the fix -- not here under a hash nobody can read.
artifacts/

# Nightly-only build state, and this package's own lock. The lock is not
# committed because the package is not part of the workspace's dependency
# promise: nothing downstream builds it, `cargo deny` at the root does not
# range over it, and pinning it would add a second lockfile to keep current
# for no consumer's benefit.
target/
Cargo.lock
coverage/
